                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "[V2G20-1001] All certificate validations shall be carried out in conformance with IETF RFC 5280 and ITU-T X.509. During certificate validation, each certificate shall be checked for conformance with the appropriate profile in Annex B. All requirements from Annex B shall be met for the appropriate certificate profile. The EVCC and the SECC shall cache certificate validation results during one service session.",
            "block_bbox": [
                68,
                1044,
                1053,
                1174
            ],
            "block_id": 13,
            "block_order": 13,
            "group_id": 13,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    68.0,
                    1044.0
                ],
                [
                    1053.0,
                    1044.0
                ],
                [
                    1053.0,
                    1174.0
                ],
                [
                    68.0,
                    1174.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "NOTE 20 The certificate validation includes checking the following.",
            "block_bbox": [
                69,
                1196,
                695,
                1221
            ],
            "block_id": 14,
            "block_order": 14,
            "group_id": 14,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    69.0,
                    1196.0
                ],
                [
                    695.0,
                    1196.0
                ],
                [
                    695.0,
                    1221.0
                ],
                [
                    69.0,
                    1221.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "a) The content of a leaf certificate has not been altered after issue. This means it is possible to check and confirm the signature up to the trust anchor level and thus the integrity of the signed content.",
            "block_bbox": [
                284,
                1227,
                1051,
                1300
            ],
            "block_id": 15,
            "block_order": 15,
            "group_id": 15,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    284.0,
                    1227.0
                ],
                [
                    1051.0,
                    1227.0
                ],
                [
                    1051.0,
                    1300.0
                ],
                [
                    284.0,
                    1300.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "b) The signature up to the trust anchor level is not compromised (none of the certificates have been revoked). Certificate revocation is checked via the OCSP response (or CRL, if allowed for that particular certificate) as detailed in 7.7.3.1 and 7.7.3.3.",
            "block_bbox": [
                284,
                1302,
                1052,
                1376
            ],
            "block_id": 16,
            "block_order": 16,
            "group_id": 16,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    284.0,
                    1302.0
                ],
                [
                    1052.0,
                    1302.0
                ],
                [
                    1052.0,
                    1376.0
                ],
                [
                    284.0,
                    1376.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "c) The validity period of each certificate in the chain up to the trust anchor has not yet elapsed.",
            "block_bbox": [
                284,
                1378,
                1054,
                1425
            ],
            "block_id": 17,
            "block_order": 17,
            "group_id": 17,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    284.0,
                    1378.0
                ],
                [
                    1054.0,
                    1378.0
                ],
                [
                    1054.0,
